	abstract = {Russell's paradox is the most famous of the logical orset-theoretical paradoxes. Also known as the Russell-Zermelo paradox,the paradox arises within na{\"\i}ve set theory by considering the setof all sets that are not members of themselves. Such a set appears tobe a member of itself if and only if it is not a member of itself.Hence the paradox.}}

