	abstract = {Philosophy of language - Wittgenstein, Semantics, Pragmatics: Frege's theory of meaning, for all its sophistication, relied on an unsatisfactory account of thoughts as abstract objects. The Tractatus did not have to deal with such a problem, because it treated meaning---and language altogether---independently of the ways in which language is actually used by human beings. Less than 10 years after the work's completion, however, Wittgenstein came to believe that this dimension of language is of paramount importance. Without some account of it, he now thought, the entire system of the Tractatus would collapse like a house of cards. In writings and teachings from 1930 on, accordingly, he emphasized}}

